  "query_preview": "..\nKey Message 1)\nHigh pressure continues to provide calm winds and clear skies this\nmorning. The only exception is where some valley fog is occurring \nacross portions of southern Ohio and northern Kentucky. Temperatures \nare falling into the mid 30s as of this writing, with the local \nridgetops the warmest and local valleys/sheltered areas the coolest.\nTemperatures continue to fall toward 32 degrees and lower into \ndaybreak. \n\nThe center of the high pressure shifts east of the region today, but\nthe only weather influence will be a light wind out of the southeast\nor east. Confidence remains high that dry conditions will persist\nthrough the entire week. Temperatures moderate back to near normal\nMonday.\n\nA weak upper level system may bring a few mid to upper level clouds\nThursday and Friday, but another ridge builds by the beginning of\nnext weekend.",
